  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to African National Public Health Institutes Programme - Support to PHI TEI and Workshop Preparation Preparation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;This assignment will support the analysis, formulation and communication about the regional programme &#xbf;Support to African Public Health Institutes&#xbf; programme, funded by INTPA under the regional MIP 2021-2027; as well as the communication about the Team Europe programmes within the framework of the Team Europe Initiative to Support African Public Health Institutes (TEI PHI). The Team Europe Approach covers the EU&#xbf;s cooperation with Sub-Saharan Africa in a coherent and coordinated comprehensive manner.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The envisaged interventions on support to African PHIs are expected to complement the already existing support provided to African PHIs and will cover the needs for a better harmonisation, alignment and coordination at regional and continental level.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The consultancy services will be provided to the European commission, mainly to headquarters in Brussels (INTPA A2/G4), the EU Delegation to the African Union and the EU Delegations in the countries participating in the programme (Burundi, CAR, Chad, DRC, Guinea Bissau, Guinea Conakry, Malawi Nigeria, Rwanda, Zimbabwe). In addition, the consultancy services will be provided in close collaboration with the Swedish International Development Cooperation Agency (SIDA)/ the Public Health Agency of Sweden (PHAS), who will lead the preparation, the conduct and the follow-up of the &#xbf;Support to African National Public Health Institutes programme components formulation workshop (PHI formulation workshop) in dialogue with Africa CDC Department &#xbf;National Public Health Institutes and Research (PHIR)&#xbf;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The objective of the present Terms of Reference is to analyse/summarise, harmonise, the content of the components of the INTPA funded Program to Support African Public Health Institutes and support the preparation of a three-day workshop in Addis Ababa (briefing notes, presentations, communication materials etc).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;In addition, consultancy services will be provided to support the Team Europe Initiative &#xbf;Support to Public Health Institutes in SSA&#xbf; (TEI PHI): to finalise/update the key documents of the TEI PHI (concept note, mapping, joint intervention logic, monitoring framework) as well as prepare communication and visibility materials to communicate about the TEI PHI to Africa CDC and other key stakeholders about the ongoing TEI PHI programmes.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
